    options: [["Personal notes", "An individual testing a regular meeting routine", "Recording minutes, meeting length and imported files"], ["Academic individual account", "An eligible person using Pro without workspace features", "School identity and current workspace membership"], ["Nonprofit team", "A validated organization buying Business access", "TechSoup approval, annual redemption and renewal costs"]],
    sections: [
      ["Choose individual or workspace access before the offer", "Draw a simple map of who creates notes, who owns the account and who needs to manage other members. A personal study workflow can be very different from an organization sharing customer conversations. Test the sharing arrangement with appropriate sample material and ask the provider which package fits it. Compare only offers for that account structure. A lower individual rate has limited value if the project depends on administrative or collaboration capabilities that require a different purchase."],
      ["Count live recordings and imports separately", "Create a month of expected work using your calendar and the recordings already waiting to be processed. Include long conversations, follow-ups and any files supplied by colleagues. Test an example of each rather than relying on one short live meeting. Compare the limits that would stop the workflow first and allow room for a busy week. This makes the price comparison reflect the actual recording process instead of an assumed number of transcript pages or finished summaries."],
      ["Prepare program approval before changing an existing account", "Check which email and subscription already hold the material you need before applying for a special price. Read the provider's account-transition instructions and ask support to resolve an eligibility mismatch before cancelling or rebuilding anything. Keep the approval, intended plan and purchase period together. For an organization, have the billing owner compare any program access cost with the complete subscription commitment. Do not infer a permanent entitlement from a single code or another user's approval."],
      ["Treat renewal as a separate purchasing decision", "Record the date, ordinary price and any steps needed to renew a program benefit before the first payment. Review whether the account will still need the same capacity and collaboration at that point. If a coupon is rejected, check the plan, account status and exact code formatting with support instead of completing an order at an unexpected amount. Keep exports of important work in the format your team uses so a future plan change is a deliberate decision."],
    ],
    redeem: ["Choose individual Pro or the required Business workspace using Otter's official plan comparison.", "For education access, use the Student & Teacher link on the eligible account; for nonprofit pricing, obtain TechSoup validation first.", "Follow the approved purchase route and confirm the selected plan, annual or monthly period and any account transition with support.", "Inspect the final order and record ordinary renewal pricing and any program reauthorization needed."],
    eligibility: [["Education account", "The Student & Teacher program concerns individual Pro and does not include Workspace features."], ["Nonprofit approval", "The official nonprofit route requires TechSoup validation and approved Business redemption."], ["Regional promotions", "Check card-country and account restrictions before comparing a local promotion with an ordinary quote."]],
    troubleshooting: [["An education offer is unavailable in a workspace", "Review the program's individual-account restrictions and ask the provider to help with the correct account setup."], ["A nonprofit code is invalid", "Check accidental spaces, annual Business selection and account status. Existing paid accounts should follow the provider's support-led transition instructions."]],
    notes: ["Official sources distinguish individual education pricing from TechSoup-approved nonprofit Business access.", "The pricing page contains billing and regional promotions. No reusable public code or worldwide promotional price was established by this guide."],
    faqs: [["Does Otter's student discount include workspace features?", "The reviewed program explicitly excludes Workspace features and concerns individual Pro. Compare an ordinary workspace package if centralized team access is essential."], ["How do nonprofits get an Otter.ai discount?", "The official route is registration and charitable-status validation through TechSoup, followed by approved Business redemption. Otter does not describe a public nonprofit code anyone can use."], ["Does an Otter nonprofit discount renew automatically?", "Official help says to obtain the applicable TechSoup renewal benefit and contact Otter for active-plan handling. Without the nonprofit renewal, the plan can renew at the regular Business rate."], ["Why is a lower Otter promotional price missing?", "Check the offer's account, billing period and regional payment conditions. Some pricing-page promotions require an India-issued card; confirm your actual order total."]],
